---
import data from '../../../public/physscope/benchmark.json';
const levels = ['Easy','Medium','Hard'] as const;
const best = Object.fromEntries(levels.map(level=>[level,Math.max(...data.models.map(m=>m.difficulty[level].score))]));
---
<section id="results" class="phys-section">
  <div id="leaderboard" class="phys-heading-row"><div><p class="phys-kicker">05 / V3 LEADERBOARD</p><h2>Compare performance by difficulty.</h2></div><span class="phys-badge">Report snapshot</span></div>
  <p class="phys-section-intro">Mean total score T on a 0–100 scale; higher is better. Select a difficulty to reorder the models and compare their scores. These scores are not success rates.</p>
  <div class="phys-board-controls" role="group" aria-label="Rank models by difficulty">
    {['Overall',...levels].map(level=><button type="button" data-ranking={level} aria-pressed={level==='Overall'}>{level}</button>)}
  </div>
  <p id="phys-ranking-status" class="phys-note" role="status">Ranked by Overall mean total score · all 40 tasks</p>
  <div class="phys-ranking-chart" aria-label="Model scores for selected difficulty">
    {data.models.map(model=><div class="phys-ranking-row" data-model={model.name}><span>{model.name}</span><div class="phys-ranking-track"><div style={`width:${model.overall}%`}></div></div><strong>{model.overall.toFixed(2)}</strong><small>n = {model.n}</small></div>)}
  </div>
  <div class="phys-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Full model leaderboard, scroll horizontally on small screens">
    <table class="phys-board-table">
      <caption>V3 mean total scores by difficulty. Bold marks the best score in each column; n is the number of scored videos.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Rank</th><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Overall</th>{levels.map(l=><th scope="col">{l}</th>)}<th scope="col">Physical success / all</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{data.models.map((model,i)=><tr data-model={model.name}><td data-rank>{i+1}</td><th scope="row">{model.name}</th><td><span class:list={{'phys-best':i===0}}>{model.overall.toFixed(2)}</span><small>n = {model.n}</small></td>{levels.map(level=><td><span class:list={{'phys-best':model.difficulty[level].score===best[level]}}>{model.difficulty[level].score.toFixed(2)}</span><small>n = {model.difficulty[level].n}</small></td>)}<td>{model.passed}/{model.n}<small>{model.successPercent.toFixed(2)}%</small></td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="phys-note">Overall is the mean across all available videos, not an unweighted average of the three difficulty means. Cosmos3 has 158 videos: P5 seed 45 and P13 seed 42 are missing; missing samples are not assigned zero. All other models have 160 videos.</p>
  <details class="phys-protocol" open>
    <summary>Scoring protocol & data provenance</summary>
    <div class="phys-method-notes">
      <div><h3>Consistency gates physical evaluation</h3><p>C is the Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct temporal-consistency score over eight sampled frames. When C ≥ 80, T = 0.15 × C + 0.85 × P. Otherwise, physical evaluation is skipped and T = 0.15 × C. P comes from task-specific physical evaluators.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Physical success is a separate measure</h3><p>Success requires all necessary metrics to be measurable and individually meet their task thresholds: 80 by default, provisionally 65 for P21 and 50 for P48. It is not a threshold on mean T. Extraction failures retain their recorded scores without being treated as proof of a physical violation.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="phys-note">Source: V3 detailed evaluation report, re-aggregated September 29, 2026 from the September 21 snapshot. No models or evaluators were rerun. Simulation first-frame videos and 16 control videos are excluded. This table follows the report’s V3 protocol; the manuscript’s method description remains in progress.</p>
    <a class="phys-data-link" href="/physscope/benchmark.json" download>Download task & leaderboard data (JSON) ↓</a>
  </details>
</section>
<script>
  import data from '../../../public/physscope/benchmark.json';
  type Level = 'Overall' | 'Easy' | 'Medium' | 'Hard';
  const chart = document.querySelector('.phys-ranking-chart')!;
  const body = document.querySelector('.phys-board-table tbody')!;
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-ranking]').forEach(button=>{
    button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
      const level = button.dataset.ranking as Level;
      const score = (model: typeof data.models[number]) => level === 'Overall' ? model.overall : model.difficulty[level].score;
      const sorted = [...data.models].sort((a,b)=>score(b)-score(a));
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-ranking]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button)));
      sorted.forEach((model,i)=>{
        const row = [...chart.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-model]')].find(r=>r.dataset.model===model.name)!;
        row.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.phys-ranking-track > div')!.style.width = `${score(model)}%`;
        row.querySelector('strong')!.textContent = score(model).toFixed(2);
        row.querySelector('small')!.textContent = `n = ${level === 'Overall' ? model.n : model.difficulty[level].n}`;
        chart.append(row);
        const tableRow = [...body.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-model]')].find(r=>r.dataset.model===model.name)!;
        tableRow.querySelector('[data-rank]')!.textContent=String(i+1);
        body.append(tableRow);
      });
      const taskCount = data.tasks.filter(t=>level==='Overall'||t.difficulty===level).length;
      document.querySelector('#phys-ranking-status')!.textContent = `Ranked by ${level} mean total score · ${taskCount} tasks`;
      chart.setAttribute('aria-label',`Model mean total scores: ${level}`);
    });
  });
</script>
